  "assessment": "The change introduces four new renderer modules (`csv_out.py`, `html_out.py`, `json_out.py`, `summary.py`) that replace or supplement the reporting logic. These implementations correctly handle the refund subtraction by checking for `kinds.REFUND` and subtracting the amount from the running total, satisfying the core business requirement where previous renderers were failing to account for refunds properly.\n\nThe structural checks passed, and acceptance tests confirmed 8/8 successful runs with no failures or vetoes, indicating the new modules integrate correctly with the existing test suite and `run.py` logic. The CSV output aligns its total line columns (`id,date,kind,amount_cents`) with the data rows, ensuring the reconciliation job can parse it correctly.",
